00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:51.773
It's incredible.

00:04:51.773 --> 00:04:53.720
It's in theater starting tomorrow.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.780
So Chris, Bryce, and Jeff

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.800
like what brought you back
to do another "Jurassic World"?

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.030
- Well, I mean, this is a, this is

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:05.130
this is the finale of the
"Jurassic World" trilogy.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.760
And so we've done three
"Jurassic World" films

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.230
but it also uniquely is wrapping

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:13.440
up the "Jurassic Park"
trilogy in the same movie.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.370
So really it's a finale for
both of these trilogies.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.387
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:17.387 --> 00:05:18.480
- And so you've had the,

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.783
the legacy cast of, of
course, Mr. Jeff Goldblum.

00:05:21.783 --> 00:05:22.616
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:22.616 --> 00:05:23.680
- Sam Neil and Laura Dern as you,

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:24.740
as you saw in the video,

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:29.060
BD Wong, all from the
original film coming back in

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:31.030
and it's really just this
extraordinary finale.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.190
And so it's, this is our, our
last this is like, you know

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.200
kind of the Swan song as the

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.660
as these characters and
really the grand finale

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.990
like you would expect to
see maybe at a, you know

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.503
a firework show or something.

00:05:42.503 --> 00:05:43.430
It just like it.

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:46.240
The minute they, the
minute the movie starts

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.620
it just explodes for two
straight hours as you saw it.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.757
- [Kelly] It does. It's
so like intense, yeah.

00:05:50.757 --> 00:05:52.990
But what, what brought you back?

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:56.260
- I mean, all of the things
that Chris was saying

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:59.760
it's pretty crazy to actually be a part

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.800
of the Jurassic franchise at all.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:02.820
- [Kelly] It's like the best.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:03.653
- [Bryce] It's insane.

00:06:03.653 --> 00:06:06.890
I was, I was 12 years old when
the original "Jurassic Park"

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.200
came out in 1993.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.960
Chris was 13 years old.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.390
We both saw it opening
weekend and it totally

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.960
changed my life.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.470
Because it made me feel like, oh my gosh

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:19.400
there's something possible at the movies

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.474
that is impossible everywhere else.

00:06:21.474 --> 00:06:22.307
- Yeah.

00:06:22.307 --> 00:06:24.230
- [Bryce] And so to get
to be a part of this,

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.460
of this franchise and then now,

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:28.570
with the legacy cast
coming back and wrapping

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:33.030
up, like Chris said, you know
both of those stories that,

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.450
you know, one of them
got started 30 years ago.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.330
I mean, it is a huge honor.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.620
- [Kelly] It was so clever too.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.200
How it all, how everybody
ran into each other,

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.220
how everybody was, it wasn't like forced.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.780
I was like, how are they gonna play this?

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:46.260
I was like, it was interesting.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.040
What brought you back, down there?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:48.873
(Kelly chuckles)

00:06:48.873 --> 00:06:49.706
- Well, I wouldn't have missed it

00:06:49.706 --> 00:06:54.141
for the world to be with Sam
and Laura again, you know?

00:06:54.141 --> 00:06:55.405
(audience applauding)

00:06:55.405 --> 00:06:56.840
Thank God.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.370
They changed my life.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.073
I'd be a different person
if I'd never met them.

00:07:00.073 --> 00:07:02.440
They're great artists and great people.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.970
And then Colin Trevorrow,

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:05.870
who wrote along with Emily Carmichael,

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:09.900
devised this very good way
to bring us all together.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.130
I'd been a fan of hers.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.900
I'd been a fan of his.
Campbell Scott is in it.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.593
Dichen Lachman. Omar Sy is back.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.230
And it's just a great cast.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.990
And Steven Spielberg is
still the godfather, you know

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:23.060
watching over the whole thing

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.770
from the start to the
finish, and over the decades

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.860
I'd seen people come up
to me and you know, go,

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:31.344
oh my kids have seen it a hundred times,

00:07:31.344 --> 00:07:33.010
it's meant so much to us.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:34.550
I just love everything about it.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.720
- Yeah. I agree. I agree.
(audience applauding)

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.910
It's a family favorite,
like, and it's generational.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.410
That's what's so cool about it.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:41.900
So y'all are new.

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:44.540
And I was gonna say, DeWanda,
I love your character.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.155
I was like, oh, she gon' be badass.

00:07:46.155 --> 00:07:47.640
(DeWanda laughs)

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:49.170
I was like very excited about it.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.470
Did you love like becoming a part of this?

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.730
- Yeah. It's a, to your point.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:55.570
I mean, it's the greatest
franchise of all time.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:58.930
And I just feel really
fortunate that I was like

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:02.100
back in this beyond epic way, you know

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.550
bringing back the legacy characters.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.580
I just, I feel very, very grateful. Yeah.

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:07.413
- [Kelly] Yeah. And Mamoudou,

00:08:07.413 --> 00:08:08.600
like this is your first
time doing this too.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:10.300
So like, what was it
like to be a part of it?

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.700
- It was nuts.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:12.900
- [Kelly] Is it kind of intimidating?

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.780
'coz you're walking on
set and you're like, okay.

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:17.320
- Yeah. My first day on
set was with Laura and Sam

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.420
and you know I grew up with them watching.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:21.560
This was the first like big blockbuster

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.660
movie I ever saw as a kid.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:26.590
So to see them and I admired
them as actors forever

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:28.830
as a kid and as an adult to see them

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.670
as those characters and work opposite them

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:33.390
I constantly found myself
just like, wait, am I

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:34.420
am I really here?

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:35.790
Is this a real thing?

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:37.850
But they really made
it just so comfortable

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.550
and a really pleasant
experience, as did these guys.

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:42.950
- [Kelly] Oh that's awesome.

